note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note HOST STAND-IN for native/nvrm/context.om, for host trace tests only. It defines the names
note launch.om uses (nvfull nvchan nvalloc nvsend nvwait nverr nvfault nvstage) without opening any
note device: buffers are anonymous private mappings (mapnew -1 0 bytes 3 34). nvsend calls fkdev
note (tests/host-trace/fakedev.om, composed after launch.om because it reads launch.om globals). Nothing here is a GPU observation;
note timings recorded around it are host timings of this stand-in.
note fkmode: 0 normal, 1 nvsend fails, 2 completion never arrives (nvwait times out),
note 3 a wrong completion mark (gblaunch sets nvfault).
global nverr long 1
global nvfault uchar 1
global nvstage uint 1
global fkmode uint 1
global fksz ulong 8
global fkn ulong 1
fn nvfull to bool
ret true
end
fn nvchan to bool
ret true
end
fn nvalloc want ulong cached bool to long
m = mapnew -1 0 want 3 34
n = get fkn 0
if lt n 8
put fksz n want
end
put fkn 0 add n 1
ret m
end
fn nvsend m long off ulong words uint to bool
if eq get fkmode 0 1
put nverr 0 -5
ret false
end
if eq get fkmode 0 2
ret true
end
mark = uint 1145324612
if eq get fkmode 0 3
mark = uint 1
end
fkdev mark
ret true
end
note nvwait polls the mark with a 20 microsecond host sleep between reads, at most 50 reads.
fn nvwait m long off ulong value uint budget ulong to bool
for i ulong 50
if eq mapget m off 4 ulong value
ret true
end
s = sleepns 20000
end
put nverr 0 -110
ret false
end
